> factor (x - 1)^3*(x + 2)^2
factor (x - 1)^3*(x + 2)^2
  = (x - 1)^3*(x + 2)^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^12 - 1
factor x^12 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)*(x^4 - x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor (x^2 + 1)^2*(x - 1)
factor (x^2 + 1)^2*(x - 1)
  = (x - 1)*(x^2 + 1)^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^4 + 4
factor x^4 + 4
  = (x^2 + 2x + 2)*(x^2 - 2x + 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor x^2 + x + 1
factor x^2 + x + 1
  = x^2 + x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor (x^3 - 2)^2
factor (x^3 - 2)^2
  = (x^3 - 2)^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> gcd (x - 1)^3, (x - 1)^2
gcd (x - 1)^3, (x - 1)^2
  = (x - 1)^2
    = x^2 - 2x + 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> lcm (x - 1)^3, (x - 1)^2
lcm (x - 1)^3, (x - 1)^2
  = (x - 1)^3
    = x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x - 1
  check: both divide it exactly
